or opinions on standard of care."\n\n**Step 6 — Reaffirm the Therapeutic Relationship**:\n"Right now, the most important thing is your health and your recovery. I am proposing treatments that have strong evidence for improving function and reducing pain. Can we focus our energy on that plan? I believe there is still meaningful improvement possible for you, and I want to help you get there."\n\n**Documentation**:\n- Document the patient\'s statements verbatim in the medical record\n- Document your response and the boundaries set\n- Note the clinical rationale for declining to opine on another physician\'s care\n- Consider notifying risk management if the patient explicitly threatens litigation against you\n- Continue providing standard of care treatment regardless of litigation threats',
